Looking at the video sequence: around the 12:30 mark, the camera wearer opens the wall oven, uses a towel to pull out the black baking tray with the roasted sweet potatoes, closes the oven door, and then sets the tray down on the gas stovetop (hob) — you can see it resting on the burner grates next to the toaster. The tray remains there while the person moves on to preparing the salad at the dining table.

So the tray is no longer in the oven, sink, or on a counter — it's sitting on the hob to cool.

